  "summary": "FORWARD THINKING DEVELOPER ☛ INTRODUCING CLIENT SIDE MVC\n\nI read development blogs and articles often to educate myself on the latest technology, trends, and tools.  A few years ago I read how the web application industry was going client side MVC for optimal rendering and performance.  The fact that you could have the client render everything and only require the server for sending and retrieving data was different from the way the application I worked on was written.  \n\nI introduced this concept to my manager and now we always take page-rendering performance into account when considering new development.  The faster I can make a page render the better user experience a client will have.  \n\nClient side MVC really helps when it comes to SaaS (software as a service) applications.  You don’t want your bandwidth being taken up by a bunch of markup you need to send back to the client.  If you want your application to scale up without taking a performance hit, the key is to reduce unneeded data being passed back and forth by allowing the client to cache markup templates.\n\nIn this position, as with every position I find myself, I continue to look for ways to maximize efficiency using the latest technology for the benefit of all stakeholders.\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\n\n➢\tProgramming Languages: VB.NET, C#, SQL\n➢\tWeb Technologies: JavaScript, Angular.JS, Node.JS JQuery, Mustache, EJS, AJAX, JSON, XML, REST API's \n➢\tWeb Design: HTML5, XML, CSS3, Bootstrap, Polymer\n➢\tDatabases: MySQL, MongoDB, SQL Server \n➢\tTest Frameworks: Grunt, Mocha\n➢\tOperating Systems: Windows, Windows Server, Mac OSX, Linux & Unix \n➢\tVersion Control Tools: CVS, Github, \n➢\tDevelopment Tool (IDE): Visual Studio, Sublime Text, Cordova/Phonegap\n➢\tSoftware: Photoshop, Visual Basic 6, Microsoft Office Suite\n\nLET'S CONNECT\n\nMy goal is to continue to push myself to stay on the leading edge of technology in my field and I am always interested in connecting with like-minded professionals.",
