    "description": "As Senior Software Engineer, I am charged with developing, evaluating, and executing code changes based on analysis and understanding of the requirements, non-functional specifications, deployment environment, and end-users’ needs. \n\nStrategies include:\n\n•\tDesigning, coding, and initiating unit test suites for use in continuous build system in order to maximize efficiency, coverage, and overall testing effectiveness (e.g. developed complex Async Javascript node.js wrapper of tedious to ensure that multiple SQL queries could be run and returned in one call back function).\n•\tConfiguring and maintaining HIPPA Practice Management and EMR software utilizing a range of robust applications such as VB.NET, C#, SQL, Javascript, and HTML/CSS. \n•\tDeveloping strong orientation with analyzing, designing, and executing EDI Scripts that read files from a SQL Server database and send/receive via SFTP, Dial-up, and HTTPS protocols.\n•\tImplementing a node.js server that interfaced with a SQL back end to calculate 64 Meaningful Use Measures for CMS Stage 2 Certification.\n•\tConverting code for Ruby Github project (https://github.com/pophealth/quality-measure-engine) to node.js, including implementing mustache and ejs templating.\n",
